sw: page count and page numbers that the user sees do not wrap after 65535 pages.

The layout stores the page count and each page's physical number as sal_uInt16. A DOCX of about
98,600 pages (docx-text 50 MB) reported 33,075 pages (98,611 mod 65,536) in the status bar, the
statistics, the PageCount field and the API, and PDF export and printing stopped after page 33,075.

HstPageCount / HstPhyPageNum / HstVirtPageNum (new hstpagecount.cxx) count the page frames
instead, and are used where the count or the number reaches the user:
- status bar "Page X of Y" (SwVisiblePageNumbers is widened to sal_uInt32);
- document statistics (Word Count, File - Properties, the PageCount field);
- the controller's PageCount property;
- the pages prepared for printing and PDF export (CalcPagesForPrint takes sal_uInt32).
The Go To Page dialog (svx, sal_uInt16) offers at most page 65535 instead of the wrapped count.
The stored 16-bit numbers inside the layout are unchanged.

Hook: sw/inc/viewsh.hxx, sw/source/core/view/{viewsh,vprint}.cxx, sw/source/uibase/uiview/view2.cxx,
sw/source/uibase/uno/{unotxdoc,unotxvw}.cxx, sw/source/core/doc/DocumentStatisticsManager.cxx,
sw/Library_sw.mk; logic in sw/inc/hstpagecount.hxx, sw/source/core/layout/hstpagecount.cxx.
Test: CppunitTest_sw_core_layout testPageCountAbove65535Pages.
